title: "FGCS Quantum Resource Benchmark: Resource-Aware Amplitude Amplification with QAOA and Classical References"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Erkalkan
    given-names: Ercan
    affiliation: "Marmara University, Vocational School of Technical Sciences, Department of Electronics and Automation, Artificial Intelligence Operator Program"
version: 1.0.0
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/ErcanErkalkan/FGCS-Quantum-Resource-Benchmark"
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - amplitude amplification
  - QAOA
  - Max-Cut
  - hybrid quantum-classical systems
  - reproducible benchmarking
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package for a resource-aware weighted Max-Cut benchmark that
  separates operational target construction, amplitude-amplification configuration,
  logical resource modeling, ideal-statevector QAOA, and classical reference methods.
  The package includes exact micro-instance ground truth, fixed-density random and
  structured graph coverage, inference tables, resource-sensitivity studies,
  generated figures/tables, tests, and fail-closed preflight validation. It makes no
  hardware-speedup or quantum-advantage claim.
